    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amblycipitidae/liobagrus_somjinensis.htm",
      "html": "<p>L. somjinensis is restricted to rivers flowing to the west coast and Geogeum Island, the Somjin, Dongin and Tamjin rivers (Kim S-h, et al. 2023).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amblycipitidae/liobagrus_somjinensis.htm",
      "html": "<p>Distinguished from its congeners by the following characters: a relatively long dorsal spine (7.3–12.4 % SL) and outer mental barbel (15.3–21.6 % SL), and a short distance from dorsal-fin insertion to adipose-fin origin (13.5–22.0 % SL).</p><p>Colouration: a broad yellowish, vertical, crescent-shaped band in the middle of the caudal fin; deep black colouration on the outer margin of the dorsal, anal and caudal fins.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amblycipitidae/liobagrus_somjinensis.htm",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: –ensis, suffix denoting place: Somjin River, South Korea, the type locality.</p>"
    },
